Registers kept as singles: a host's quick ways for single precision (the Tab5 firmware's, on the P4's
single-precision FPU) keep a register's value as an exact single in sb[], so that it isn't converted to a double
and back by each instruction; fpget makes the double when tiny386's code reads it (the single kept: the same
value), fpset and FRSTOR forget the single, FNSAVE makes the doubles first.

